          "page": 4,
          "section": "2.1 Material production and sample preparation",
          "quote": "Thirty grams of the resulting alloyed powder were consolidated through SPS-625, SINTER LAND INC., Chiyoda, Japan) employing the subsequent thermal profile: heating at rates of 100 C/min from to 600 C, 50 C/min from 600 to 900 C, and 25 C/min from 900 to 1050 C. Isothermal treatment at 1050 C under 30 MPa pressure for 10 min ensured complete densification and inhibited detrimental microstructure coarsening.",
